 Short Brief 
👉 The code finds the length of the last word in a string by:

Removing extra spaces using trim()
Traversing the string from the end
Counting characters until a space is found
Returning the count


✅ Key Idea
👉 Move backwards and count characters of the last word.

✅ Complexity

Time Complexity: O(n) → single pass through string
Space Complexity: O(1) → no extra space used

Thank You
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLastWord(String s) {
        s=s.trim();
        int length=0;
        for(int i=s.length()-1;i>=0;i--){
            if(s.charAt(i)!=' '){
                length++;
            }else{
                break;
            }
        }
        return length;
        
    }
}
